        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.674,
            0.804,
            0.695
          ],
          "content": "The temperature of a body tells us how hot or cold it is."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.699,
            0.884,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": " The three most-used scales of temperature are: (a) the Celsius scale, (b) the Fahrenheit scale, and (c) the Kelvin scale. The units of temperature in these scales are (a) degree Celsius, denoted by °C, (b) degree Fahrenheit, denoted by °F, and (c) kelvin, denoted by K. The SI unit for temperature is kelvin."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.807,
            0.883,
            0.827
          ],
          "content": "A clinical thermometer is used for measuring body temperature."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.832,
            0.883,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": " Normal temperature of a healthy human adult is taken to be $3 7 . 0   ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$ or $9 8 . 6 ~ \\mathrm { ^ \\circ F }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.876,
            0.884,
            0.915
          ],
          "content": " Laboratory thermometers typically have a temperature range from $- 1 0 \\; ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$ to $1 1 0   ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ,$"
        },
